## Reviewer disagreements (not applied)

- fa-a 2, 3, and 6 undo RULEBOOK R3. The English source still has “generally impose”, “maximum compensation”, and “a substantial severance”; the standing rule is to keep the softened Persian.
- fa-a 11 and fa-b 14 treat U+200B and the Q16–Q20 body lines as editor noise. They are structural copies of the Korean source. The checker fails if the counts move.
- fa-b 17’s renumber treats a gap that is in the English and Korean sources. Only the plural verb was a Persian error.
- fa-a 12 is right that the label must not argue with the business-tax article. Deleting the digit 10 is not possible: `numbers FAIL missing 10` on that link. Kept «مادهٔ 3؛ عنوان منبع: مادهٔ 10».
- fa-a 14 is right that «TWD 1.57M» is English notation. The pin overrides the rewrite.
- fa-b 18 suggested «دو سوم» in words. Kept «2/3» and added «از» («2/3 یا بیشتر از حق رأی») so the fraction stays tied to the voting rights and the digits still parse.
- fa-b 29 suggested «یک رأی» in words. «1 نفر 1 رأی» is gone; «هر سهامدار 1 رأی دارد» remains. After that change, 018 numbers are `sourceCount=25 targetCount=25`. Replacing the remaining digit with «یک» was not required for the checker and was not done.

Not expanded: 007’s paragraph after the ten grounds still summarizes the constitutional judgment without the “considerable period” test. That sentence was not the quoted row (the quoted wording is in the FAQ and in section 4, both fixed). Adding the test there would be new wording in an unflagged block.

